patrone-hyperv-setup (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Its name is now Virtual Machine Setup, in the window, the dialog's
    titles, the app's entry, the password prompt and the package's
    description: Microsoft's trademark guidelines keep its marks, Hyper-V
    among them, out of product names (docs/COMPLIANCE.md, item 15). The
    text still says what it's for. The package, program, units and app ID
    keep their names, which a rename would have to migrate.
  * A line in the dialog and the description: Hyper-V and Windows are
    trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies.
  * To leave room for it at 1024 by 768, the size Hyper-V's basic window
    often has: the first page's opening line is one line, the rows are a
    little tighter, and the note about the VM's name is shorter.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500

